#
# ROC-RK3399-PC. One product, successive board revisions: V0.1 -> V1.1-A ->
# V1.2A, treated here as ONE board: no per-revision map, no per-revision
# directory. They are not distinguishable at runtime today -- the practical
# discriminator is the DDR model, which nothing reads.
#
# Exactly two pins differ. J20.25 and J20.26 are GPIO0_A1 / GPIO0_B4 on
# V1.1-A; on V1.2A both were taken off the expansion header to drive the new
# eDP panel's touch controller, and carry no net at the header there. Every
# other J12/J15/J20 pin is identical across revisions.
#
# The rows keep their V1.1-A Chip/Line and name BOTH states in Ref, so
# `lgpio info J20 25` shows the divergence. CAUTION: on V1.2A driving those
# lines is not a harmless no-op -- the SoC lines are live and owned by the
# touch-panel circuit, so driving them from the header disturbs the panel.
# Source: tf-xd-rk3399-pc-v1.2a-20221109-changelog.pdf -- "expansion header:
# remove the following two IO ports, used for the eDP panel's TP".
# Detail: rockchip/rk3399/schematics/roc-rk3399-pc-revision-differences.md
#
# Not an RPi pinout: four 30-pin CON30A at 2.0 mm. J12/J15/J20 are the GPIO
# headers; J21 is a PCIe breakout and is not mapped. lgpio bcm does not apply.
